@page "/"

<PageTitle>Watch This for Me</PageTitle>

<h1>Watch This for Me</h1>
<p class="lead">An AI agent that keeps an eye on the things you care about, and tells you only when something changes that matters.</p>

<div class="row g-4 my-2">
    <div class="col-md-6">
        <h5>What it does</h5>
        <ul>
            <li>You describe what to watch in plain English: a GitHub repo, a release notes page, a company's news page.</li>
            <li>It checks the source on a schedule and spots what changed since last time.</li>
            <li>AI reads each change and judges it against <em>your</em> rule, e.g. "only breaking changes or security fixes".</li>
            <li>For important changes, it can investigate further and explain what happened, citing the evidence it found.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="col-md-6">
        <h5>What it's for, and what it isn't</h5>
        <p>
            It's built for changes that need <strong>interpreting</strong>: "is this new release relevant to me?",
            "did this company announce something significant?" A plain text diff can't answer those questions.
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted">
            It isn't a price or threshold alert. Rules like "tell me when a stock drops below $400" are better served
            by a brokerage or monitoring app, which tracks exact numbers in real time.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<a class="btn btn-primary" href="watches">Go to my watches</a>
